{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>You shall not eat of it raw.</b> What is not fully roasted is called נָא in the Arabic language." "<b>Or boiled, boiled.</b> All of this is under the prohibition of <b>you shall not eat</b>." "<b>In water.</b> From where do we derive the other liquids? Scripture says: ״וּבָשֵׁל מְבֻשָׁל״ — from anywhere (Pesachim 41a)." "<b>But roasted with fire.</b> Above He decreed upon it a positive commandment, and here He added to it a negative commandment: <b>you shall not eat of it … but roasted with fire</b>." "<b>Its head upon its legs.</b> Roast it whole, all together — with its head and with its legs and with its innards; and its entrails he places inside it after they have been washed (Pesachim 74a). And the expression <b>upon its innards</b> is like the expression ״עַל צִבְאוֹתָם״ (Exodus 6) — just as ״בְּצִבְאוֹתָם״ means as they are, so too this means as it is — all of its flesh complete."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:36.161407464Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}